{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuTwoThreeNotProportional"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.ocneanu_ratio_adjacent_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.ocneanu_ratio_adjacent_ne","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.lean#L80-L101","doc":"**The exclusion at full strength.** For *every* `N`, the Ocneanu weight\nratios at `N` and at `N + 1` differ — and by `qb_shift_identity` the discrepancy\nis the same `[3]_q` at every `N`.\n\nSo the recorded reason for the route-3 exclusion — *\"the `N=2` and `N=3` traces\nare not proportional\"* — is the `N = 2` case of a fact that holds all the way\nup: no re-tuning to an adjacent `N` reproduces the weighting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.ocneanu_ratio_N2_ne_N3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.ocneanu_ratio_N2_ne_N3","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.lean#L64-L78","doc":"**The exclusion, proved.** At any real `q > 1` — the substrate sits at\n`q₀ ≈ 1.10998` — the `N = 2` and `N = 3` Ocneanu weight ratios are different.\n\nSo moving to `N = 3` does not merely add the singlet channel; it re-weights the\nchannels already in use. That is the content the exclusion row asserts, and it\nno longer rests on a sample. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.qIntBal_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.qIntBal_pos","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.lean#L53-L62","doc":"**Positivity of the canonical balanced `q`-integer at `q > 1`.**\n\nStated on `QOU.QInteger.qIntBal` rather than on the local `qb`, at the request\nof the agent working bean `qou-qint` (PR #5746): the canonical module is generic\nover a field and so carries no ordering — correctly, per §7c — which leaves\npositivity genuinely absent from it. This is the right side of the wall for it,\nand `qIntBal` is the right object to say it about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.qb_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.qb_pos","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.lean#L37-L51","doc":"**Every `q`-integer is positive at `q > 1`.** One lemma in place of a\nper-index battery: `[m]_q = (qᵐ − q⁻ᵐ)/(q − q⁻¹)` has a positive numerator\n(`qᵐ > 1 > q⁻ᵐ`) over a positive denominator (`q > 1 > q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.q_sq_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.q_sq_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/OcneanuTwoThreeSubstrate.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0}]}